# Figma MCP → React Native (coconut-app)

When the user shares a **Figma frame link**, screenshot, or asks to match a design:

## 1. Prefer Figma MCP over screenshots

- Ask for or use the **frame link** (`node-id=…`) — do not guess spacing/colors from PNG alone.
- Implement **one frame at a time** (hero, card, list section). Avoid whole-app frames.
- If MCP is available, fetch design context / variables before writing code.

## 2. Output stack (never web)

- **React Native + Expo** only: `View`, `Text`, `Pressable`, `ScrollView`, `StyleSheet.create`
- ❌ No `motion/react`, `div`, Tailwind, `className`, CSS files, or Next.js patterns
- Use `SafeAreaView` / `useSafeAreaInsets` for top and bottom padding
- Use `useTheme()` → `theme.*` for colors; never invent hex if a token exists
- Typography: `font.regular`, `font.medium`, `font.semibold`, `font.bold`, `font.black` from `lib/theme`
- Spacing/radii: `radii.*`, `space.*` from `lib/theme` when values match

## 3. Match Figma 1:1

- Copy **exact** padding, gap, font size, weight, line height, border radius, and colors from MCP context
- Map Figma auto-layout → RN flexbox (`flexDirection`, `gap`, `alignItems`, `justifyContent`)
- Prefer flex over absolute positioning unless Figma uses absolute
- Export icons/SVGs/PNG assets from Figma when MCP images are needed; don't substitute emoji

## 4. Reuse existing components

Check before creating new UI:

- `components/home/*`, `MemberAvatar`, `MerchantLogo`, `CoconutTabBar`
- `lib/home-theme.ts` for home-specific colors (wave, split orange, etc.)

Extend existing components rather than duplicating parallel versions.

## 5. Prompt pattern (for user)

```
Figma frame: [link]
Implement 1:1 in coconut-app. React Native only. Use theme tokens.
Frame: [single component name]
```
